Z||000006||william_thorniii||02-22-2000||12:35 PM||||Moocow,<P>There are hundreds of Fiero owners in MI.  Check out the MI Fiero Club webpage.  It is one of the best on the net.  Make sure that you check out FOLD there too.  That will help you locate other owners in your area. <P>Brian,<P>I lived in Flint and can tell you that you DO NOT want a Fiero from there.  The roads have pot holes deep enough to bottom a Fiero out and I am not joking.  Furthermore all of the salt that is poured on the roads kills all underbodies.  This is compounded by the fact that during the 80's most folks worked for the car manufacturers.  When you get an enourmous discount it is much more difficult to labor and toil about keeping the one you have nice.  Please note that I am not saying that all cars up there are beat up and nearly dead... but anything under $1000 would not be worth your time in my opinion.  Of course there is always an exception to every rule.  You will have talk to this guy to get a feel for if it is really a good value or if it is not worth anything as I suspect.  <P>William T. Thorn, III<P>William T. Thorn, III<P>sorry, i dont live in michigan. i live in north carolina. i found a car for sale in michigan, and was wondering if anyone was close by to either look at it (it's a $300 car, i would hate to fly there look at it and not be able to drive it or want it), new of the car.<BR>sorry for any confusion<P>brian<BR>||||reg||12
